{ "Accession" : "46617",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "48.3916022222222222" , "lng":  "-123.2558527777777778" , "Locality" : "Strongtide Islet, near Chatham Island, Victoria. W side of island, 30m WNW of communication tower, near water. Map Sheet # 92B/6. 10U 481078 536416 5m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Bottom and edges of small drying vernal pool on ruck bluff , in fairly shallow (6-10 cm deep) soil. With Plagiobothrys scouleri. Species growing adjacent: Holcus lanatus, Camassia leichtlinii, Rubus ursinus, Rosa sp., Allium cernuum, Achillea millefolium, Cytisus scoparius, Saxifraga caespitosa. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inindated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer. Several small mats, approx. 200 individuals. Total cover 0.25m2 in a 1 m x 1m (1m2) pool, no particular orientation.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Gulf Islands",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46618",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "49.9494155555555556" , "lng":  "-124.9962158333333333" , "Locality" : "F Island, small islet next to Mitlenatch Island. SE end of island, on open bluff. Map Sheet # 92F/15. 10U 356792 5534918. Island is a restricted access area within Mitlenatch Island Provincial Nature Park.",  "Ecology" : "Drying margins of vernal pool on rocky poen bluff. Soil mostly bare. Solitary pool except for scattered Carex sp., with Myosorus minimus and Plagiobothrys scouleri growing in similar adjacent habitat. Also present nearby: Claytonia perfoliata, Salix sp., Amsinkia spectabilis. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inundated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer",   "GeoSecondary" : "Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46619",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "48.3893511111111111" , "lng":  "-123.2526775" , "Locality" : "Vantreight Island, near Chatham Island, Victoria, E side of island, ~100m E of communications tower, in small rock pool. Map Sheet: 92B/6 UTM: 10U 481312 5365165 5m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Partially submerged in water at edge of small rock pool on open, flat, rocky bluff with Douglas-fir, Arbutus, Garry oak nearby. Growing solitary in pool. Adjacent species: Bromus hordeaceus, Anthoxanthum oderatum, Cynosurus echinata, Epilobium ciliatum and rumex acetosella. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inundated in winter/spring. One small mat, approx. 30 individuals. Total cover 0.04m2 in a 0.5m x 0.5m (0.25 m2) pool, no particular orientation.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46620",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "48.3234808333333333" , "lng":  "-123.5405661111111111" , "Locality" : "Rocky Point Base just S of Cape Calver, on coastal bluff 15m from high tide mark. Site is part of a restricted access area on property managed by the Dept. of National Defense (DND). Map Sheet B/5. UTM: 10U 459929 5352396 5m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Margin of small, drying vernal pool on open rocky bluff near Douglas-fir/trembling apsen/Garry oak grove. Associated species: Plagiobothrys scouleri. Vegetation growing adjacent: Tritelia hyacinthina, Bromus racemosus, Hordeum brachyantherum, Vicia sp., Trifolium variegatum. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inundated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer, Slope 5%, Aspect: North. Several small remnant fragments, approx. 200 individuals. Total cover 0.04m2 in a 1m x 1m (1m2) pool with no particular orientation.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46621",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "48.3105555555555556" , "lng":  "-123.5872222222222222" , "Locality" : "Rocky Point, Church Point, NNE Church Island and W of Church Hill, on open grassy bluff near water. Site is part of a restricted access area on property managed by the dEpt. of National Defense (DND). Map Sheet# 92B/5. UTM: 456461 5350980 5m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Bottom edges of drying vernal pool on open coastal bluff; Mainly solitary, but with scattered Plagiobothrys scouleri; Adjacent vegetation present: Festuca rubra and Poa pratense, Vulpia bromiodes, V. microstachys, Lotus formomissimus, Myosotis discolor, Aira praecox, Mimulus guttatus, Luzulu multiflora, Sagina apetala, Allium sp.  Plantago lanceolata, Armeria maritima;  Light: open, Position: crest; Moisture: inundated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer. Several small remnant mats, approx 200 individuals. Total cover 0.2m2 in a 1m x 3m (3m2) pool with an east-west orientation",   "GeoSecondary" : "Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46622",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "49.9485822222222222" , "lng":  "-124.9962158333333333" , "Locality" : "Fort Rodd Hill, 400m WNW of Fisgard Light House. A raised outcrop area with central depression to the S of the 'Battery Commander's Post' Map sheet 92B/6; UTM: 10U 356792 5534918  5m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "A 3.5x10m depression between rock outcrops, occupied 80% by Carex unilateralis. 20% open muddy ground forms habitat for Callitriche. Other scattered species in Callitriche habitat: Agrostis stolonifera, Gnaphalium palustre, Veronica peregrina, Myosurus minimus, Plagiobothrys scouleri, Camassia quamash, Alopecurus carolinianus. Light: partial . Position: crest. Moisture: inundated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer. A tiny mat of plants. Number not possible to determine without disturbing plants. Two tiny patches, 0.02m2",   "GeoSecondary" : "Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "46623",   "Family": "Callitrichaceae",  "ScientificName": "Callitriche marginata Torr.   "  , "lat":  "48.4417666666666667" , "lng":  "-123.2996361111111111" , "Locality" : "Uplands Park, Victoria. In central meadow near west-central portion of park. Map sheet:92B/6 10U 477840 5365446   6m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Vernally wet, fairly shallow bare-soil depressions in an open meadow domianted by Camassia quamash and introduced grasses (Holcus lanatus, Agrostis stolonifera, Cynosurus cristatus). With Plagiobothrys scouleri, Centaurium muhlenbergii (later in season), Lotus micranthus, Microsteris gracilis, Brodiaea cornonaria and Tritelia hyacinthina. Also, some plants growing on edge of walking trail, on top of drying mud. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inundated in winter/spring, dry (xeric) in summer. Number of individuals not possible to determine without disturbing plants, but probably several hundred present. 3-4 patches, separated from one another by 1 to sevral metres of higher ground. Each patch ~1-2m2, with total area covered by population (including unoccupied ground) ~30m2; shape and direction indistinct.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Uplands Park , Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
