{ "Accession" : "46626",   "Family": "Gentianaceae",  "ScientificName": "Centaurium muhlenbergii Raf.   "  , "lat":  "48.4417666666666667" , "lng":  "-123.2996361111111111" , "Locality" : "Uplands Park, Victoria, In central meadow near west-central portion of park. Map Sheet# 92B/6. 10U 477840 5365446  6 m NAD 83",  "Ecology" : "Vernally wet, fairly shallow bare-soil depressions in an open meadow domianted by Camassia quamash and introduced grasses (Holcus lanatus, Agrostis stolonifera, Cynosurus cristatus). With Plagiobothrys scouleri, Callitriche marginata (earlier in season), Lotus micranthus, Microsteris gracilis, Brodiaea cornonaria and Tritelia hyacinthina. Also scattered through grass on more elevated ground, and in wheel ruts. Light: open, Position: crest, Moisture: inundated in winter/spring , dry (xeric) in summer. Approx. 800 individuals. 4-5 main patches, separated from one another by 5-20m of unoccupoed meadow. Scattered over area ~50m x 20m (0.1ha) on E side of large rock outcrop and oriented in a SE-NW direction.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Uplands Park , Vancouver Island",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
