{ "Accession" : "40887",   "Family": "Liliaceae",  "ScientificName": "Erythronium grandiflorum Pursh   "  , "lat":  "50.8005555555555556" , "lng":  "-119.7480555555555556" , "Locality" : "Chase area.  On Neskainlith IR 1, NE of site described for DL96-1 (but SE-facing).",  "Ecology" : "Abundant in open meadow with occasional Pseudotsuga menziesii in the area; with Symphoricarpos albus, Crataegus douglasii, Balsamorhiza sagittata, Galium boreale, Zigadenus venenosus, Taraxacum officinale, Lupinus sericeus, Claytonia lanceolata, Lomatium dissectum, Mertensia longiflora.  At this location, bulbs were collected for stage of growth analysis, flowering and later stages (see thesis).  SE exp., slope 7 deg.  [voucher for M.Sc. thesis by D. Loewen, Department of Biology, University of Victoria, 1998].  This plant unrelated to experiments, but grew in the same area.  Collected to show striking mottled leaves (sporadic in population; cause unknown).",   "GeoSecondary" : "",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
