{ "Accession" : "408851",   "Family": "Liliaceae",  "ScientificName": "Erythronium grandiflorum Pursh   "  , "lat":  "51.7722222222222222" , "lng":  "-119.9361111111111111" , "Locality" : "Wells Gray Provincial Park, Trophy Mountain meadows, at treeline.",  "Ecology" : "SW exp., minimal slope.  Claytonia lanceolata, Valeriana sitchensis, Arnica latifolia, Erigeron peregrinus, Anemone occidentalis, Lupinus arcticus.  SITE OF TRANSPLANT EXP'T.   [voucher for M.Sc. Thesis by D. Loewen, Department of Biology, University of Victoria, 1998].  These plants came up and flowered 1 yr after whole-bulb transplant from elsewhere in meadow: top plant with small leaf (now separated) growing from appendage, probably stimulated by disturbance of transplanting; bottom plant, from bulb that came to rest sideways, not yet righted.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Wells Gray Park",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "408852",   "Family": "Liliaceae",  "ScientificName": "Erythronium grandiflorum Pursh   "  , "lat":  "51.7722222222222222" , "lng":  "-119.9361111111111111" , "Locality" : "Wells Gray Provincial Park, Trophy Mountain meadows, at treeline.",  "Ecology" : "SW exp., minimal slope.  Claytonia lanceolata, Valeriana sitchensis, Arnica latifolia, Erigeron peregrinus, Anemone occidentalis, Lupinus arcticus.  SITE OF TRANSPLANT EXP'T.   [voucher for M.Sc. Thesis by D. Loewen, Department of Biology, University of Victoria, 1998].  Top plant: came up and flowered 1 yr after whole buld transplant from elsewhere in meadow (has stunted 2nd scape that is hard to see); bottom plant, 2-leaved vegetative state missed when area was cleared for experiment (not transplanted); included to show how easy it is to overlook bulbs even when deliberately attempting to harvest every last bulb in a small area!",   "GeoSecondary" : "Wells Gray Park",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "408853",   "Family": "Liliaceae",  "ScientificName": "Erythronium grandiflorum Pursh   "  , "lat":  "51.7722222222222222" , "lng":  "-119.9361111111111111" , "Locality" : "Wells Gray Provincial Park, Trophy Mountain meadows, at treeline.",  "Ecology" : "SW exp., minimal slope.  Claytonia lanceolata, Valeriana sitchensis, Arnica latifolia, Erigeron peregrinus, Anemone occidentalis, Lupinus arcticus.  SITE OF TRANSPLANT EXP'T.   [voucher for M.Sc. Thesis by D. Loewen, Department of Biology, University of Victoria, 1998].  Top left plant: 2-leaved plant, not transplanted (see DL97-37b).  Right and bottom left plants: both cam up and flowered one yr after whole-bulb transplant from elsewhere in meadow.  Bottom left seedling: developed from seed of previous year (not transplanted).",   "GeoSecondary" : "Wells Gray Park",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
{ "Accession" : "408854",   "Family": "Liliaceae",  "ScientificName": "Erythronium grandiflorum Pursh   "  , "lat":  "51.7722222222222222" , "lng":  "-119.9361111111111111" , "Locality" : "Wells Gray Provincial Park, Trophy Mountain meadows, at treeline.",  "Ecology" : "SW exp., minimal slope.  Claytonia lanceolata, Valeriana sitchensis, Arnica latifolia, Erigeron peregrinus, Anemone occidentalis, Lupinus arcticus.  SITE OF BULB-APPENDAGE EXP'T.   [voucher for M.Sc. Thesis by D. Loewen, Department of Biology, University of Victoria, 1998].  All 3 plants grew from appendages manually separated from bulbs and replanted the previous year.  The 1-leaved and 2-leaved plants (bottom), grew from 2 appendages removed from a single bulb (genetically identical).  The top plant grew from an appendage separated from a different bulb. First direct evidence of vegetative reproduction in this species.",   "GeoSecondary" : "Wells Gray Park",  "GeoPrimary" : "British Columbia", "Country" : "Canada",  "Continent" : "North America"},
